# inc-1xr3: prove the deep water handler reads its OWN constants and still
# makes the Swim check. Place one square of deep water one step east of the
# player with wizard mode, then walk east into it. The move INTO the terrain
# is the case the defect was about: EActor still stands on the OLD square
# when EV_MOVE fires, so reading EMap->TerrainAt(EActor->x,EActor->y) saw the
# old terrain and rolled SkillCheck(0,0). Read the "Confirm enter the deep
# water? (...)" prompt and the "Swim Check: ... vs DC 10" line from the
# screen dumps.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR=logs/runs/1xr3-deep-water \
#   tools/headless.sh tools/keys/deep-water-swim.keys 20260905

@include chargen.keys

w
y
ESC # Enable wizard mode, then leave its menu without killing anything.

# One square of deep water, one step east of the player.
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT ENTER
@choose "deep water"
@dump:pool

# Walk east into it. The prompt fires while the player is still on the OLD
# square; the Swim Check fires after the step.
RIGHT
@dump:prompt
y
@dump:entered
RIGHT
@dump:second

@quit
